<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργέω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤργησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					698.4
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤργηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1160.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργός,
				ἀεργός</span>):—<i>to be unemployed, do nothing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mochl.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				625
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				426a
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>keep Sabbath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ma.</u>
				5.25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὴν ἑβδόμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					7.3.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀργοῦντες</span>”
				<i>the idle,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Trag.Adesp.
					527
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ ἀργοῦσα</span>”
				<i>lying fallow,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.6.11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFlor.</u>
				262.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργῆσαν ἤμυσε στέγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					864
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φησὶν ἀργῆσαι τὸ ἐργαστήριον</span>”
				<i>is out of work,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					27.19
				</span></i>
			; of the senses, <i>to be at rest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτὸς τῆς ὄψεως ἀργούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					903a21
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Somn.Vig.</u>
				455a30
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργήσει . . τῆς
				αὑτοῦ δημιουργίας</span>
			<i>will be unoccupied in</i> his own work, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				371c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be left undone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.3.3
			</span></i>; <i>to be fruitless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ σκέψις ἂν ἀργοῖτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hier.</u>
					9.9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
